# macOS and Xcode noise.
.DS_Store
xcuserdata/

# Local secret files. Nothing in this repository reads one today — the Teenybase
# backend that used to live under `Vaultic/backend/` has been removed — but these
# are the file shapes that hold credentials for every tool that uses them, and
# this repository did once commit a `.dev.vars` full of live secrets. Keeping the
# rule is cheap; rediscovering it the hard way is not.
.dev.vars
.env
.env.*

# Note: a `.gitignore` only stops *new* files from being tracked. `.DS_Store` and
# `Vaultic.xcodeproj/**/xcuserdata/**` are already tracked in this repository, so
# those two lines document intent rather than removing anything — they need a
# `git rm --cached` to take effect on files already committed.

# Tool state written by the `asc` CLI (release checkpoints); never source.
.asc/

# Scratch written by agent tooling next to its own config, one directory per command.
# Not source and never something to `git add` — but it lands inside the repository, so
# without this rule every `git status` carries twenty lines of it.
.reasonix/tasks/
